# Next.js 15 App Router Rules — GoodEpoch Cursor Rules Pack v1
# Applies to: Next.js 15.x with App Router
# Stack: Next.js 15, React 19, TypeScript 5.5+

## Server vs Client Components — The Core Boundary

- Server Components are the default. NEVER add 'use client' without explicit reason
- 'use client' is only justified for: browser APIs (window/document), event handlers (onClick etc),
  useState, useEffect, useReducer, useRef for DOM access, third-party libs that require client
- Never fetch data in Client Components. Fetch in Server Components, pass down as props
- Server Components can be async — use `await` directly at the top level
- When you need interactivity + data, split: parent Server Component fetches, child Client Component handles UI

## Data Fetching Patterns

- Fetch data in page.tsx or layout.tsx using async Server Components:
  ```typescript
  // app/users/page.tsx
  export default async function UsersPage() {
    const users = await db.query.users.findMany()
    return <UserList users={users} />
  }
  ```
- Use `cache()` from React for request deduplication across the component tree
- Use `unstable_cache` from next/cache for cross-request caching with tags:
  ```typescript
  const getUser = unstable_cache(
    async (id: string) => db.query.users.findFirst({ where: eq(users.id, id) }),
    ['user'],
    { tags: ['users'], revalidate: 60 }
  )
  ```
- Parallel data fetching with `Promise.all` in Server Components
- Use `Suspense` boundaries to stream in data as it resolves

## Server Actions — Mutations

- ALL form mutations use Server Actions. Never API routes for same-origin mutations:
  ```typescript
  // actions/user.ts
  'use server'
  export async function createUser(formData: FormData) {
    const parsed = createUserSchema.safeParse(Object.fromEntries(formData))
    if (!parsed.success) return { error: parsed.error.flatten() }
    await db.insert(users).values(parsed.data)
    revalidatePath('/users')
  }
  ```
- Validate ALL server action inputs with zod before processing
- Return typed responses: `{ error: string } | { data: T }` — never throw from server actions
- Use `revalidatePath` or `revalidateTag` after mutations, not `router.refresh()`
- Bind actions to forms with the `action` prop or use `startTransition` for programmatic calls

## File and Folder Conventions

- `app/` directory structure mirrors URL structure
- Required files per route: `page.tsx` (required), `layout.tsx`, `loading.tsx`, `error.tsx`, `not-found.tsx`
- `loading.tsx` creates automatic Suspense boundary — use it for skeleton UIs
- `error.tsx` must be a Client Component (`'use client'`) with reset capability
- Route groups `(group)/` for organization without affecting URL
- Private folders `_components/` for components that shouldn't be routes
- `app/api/` only for: webhooks, OAuth callbacks, third-party integrations, public APIs

## Metadata and SEO

- Export `metadata` object or `generateMetadata` function from every page:
  ```typescript
  export const metadata: Metadata = {
    title: 'Page Title',
    description: 'Page description',
    openGraph: { title: 'OG Title', images: ['/og.png'] }
  }
  ```
- Use `generateMetadata` for dynamic pages that need database data
- Configure `metadataBase` in root layout for absolute OG image URLs

## Routing and Navigation

- Use `<Link>` from `next/link` for ALL internal navigation — never `<a>` tags
- `useRouter` from `next/navigation` (not `next/router`) for programmatic navigation
- `usePathname`, `useSearchParams` for reading current URL in Client Components
- Dynamic routes: `[id]` for single, `[...slug]` for catch-all, `[[...slug]]` for optional catch-all
- `generateStaticParams` for static generation of dynamic routes

## Images and Fonts

- Use `next/image` for ALL images. Never raw `<img>` tags in App Router
- Always provide `width`/`height` or use `fill` with a sized container
- Use `next/font` for all fonts — zero layout shift, automatic self-hosting
- Priority prop on above-the-fold images: `<Image priority />`

## Middleware

- `middleware.ts` at project root for auth guards, redirects, A/B testing
- Middleware runs on edge — no Node.js APIs, no database calls
- Use `matcher` config to avoid running on static assets:
  ```typescript
  export const config = { matcher: ['/((?!_next/static|_next/image|favicon.ico).*)'] }
  ```

## Environment Variables

- `NEXT_PUBLIC_` prefix for client-exposed vars only
- All server-only vars accessed via server components/actions — never expose to client
- Validate env vars at startup with zod in `lib/env.ts`

## Performance Patterns

- Use `React.Suspense` with meaningful fallbacks at data boundaries
- `dynamic()` from `next/dynamic` for heavy client components with `ssr: false` when needed
- Static pages where possible — use `revalidate` for ISR rather than fully dynamic
- Bundle analysis: `@next/bundle-analyzer` to find large client-side imports
